  "details": "Currently non-vr users can't grab physbones through normal means. The grab gesture doesn't count as a grab, nor does grabbing with selfie expression.\n\nThe colliders are there, the collision and contacts work fine, and selfie expression already lets us move our avatar's hands somewhat freely. \n\nYes, I can see how this might get in the way, and I suggest a few things here that might help that a bit.\n\n1. A toggle in the settings, with off being the default.\n\n2. Adding it to selfie expression, and maybe only when your hands are being actively tracked.\n\n3. Same as 1, but also have an interaction toggle dedicated to non-vr users, allowing vr users to still grab and mess with your physbones.\n\nTo clarify, I'm not asking for it to count as a click, I'm asking for a feature to not effectively lock out a portion of the player base when they should be able to use it.",
